Source: azusalinux
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: azusa <dsyfb437@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3, python3-pil
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/dsyfb437/azusalinux

Package: azusa-tools
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-pil
Recommends: fastfetch
Description: AzusaLinux command-line tools
 azusa-fetch, azusa-logo, azusa-palette, azusa-apply and the wallpaper
 generators, with the shared palette and mascot under /usr/share/azusalinux.

Package: azusa-artwork
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: AzusaLinux wallpapers
 Light and dark lake landscapes and mascot illustrations for the GNOME
 wallpaper picker.

Package: azusa-settings
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, azusa-artwork, azusa-icons, fonts-inter, fonts-jetbrains-mono
Description: AzusaLinux desktop defaults
 GSettings overrides for accent colour, fonts, wallpaper and icon theme,
 plus system-wide kitty colours and a Ptyxis palette for new users.

Package: azusa-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, azusa-release (= ${binary:Version}), azusa-tools, azusa-artwork, azusa-settings, fastfetch
Description: AzusaLinux desktop (metapackage)
 Installs the AzusaLinux tools, artwork and desktop defaults on Ubuntu.

Package: azusa-icons
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, papirus-icon-theme, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0
Description: AzusaLinux system and desktop icons
 Original system launcher, device and desktop icons with matching Papirus
 folders. GNOME accent colours select a coordinated theme for each user.

Package: azusa-release
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, base-files
Description: AzusaLinux release identity
 Package-managed operating system identity and login banners. Package-specific
 dpkg diversions preserve the Ubuntu originals and protect the Azusa identity
 during base-files upgrades; removing the package restores the vendor files.
